prompt:
The brief has changed. Here is the change, in addition to everything the brief said before:

# Change 1: reservations expire

A confirmed order's reservation can now expire, for example when the customer does not complete the purchase in time. The shop reports it with a command.

- `expire(order)`: a confirmed order becomes **expired** and gives its units back to the inventory, as a cancelled order does. Refused otherwise.

`status` in the view can now also be `"expired"`. An expired order accepts no command. Everything else is as before.

The host interface is now as follows, and `host.ts` has been updated to match.

```ts
// T2 after change 1, orders and inventory with expiry: the host interface every arm implements (PT13, S91).

/** A message sent by one part of the system to another, not yet delivered. */
export interface Message {
  id: string;
  from: string;
  to: string;
  action: string;
  data: Record<string, unknown>;
}

/** The network: nothing is delivered until deliver or deliverAll is called. */
export interface Network {
  /** Every message in transit, in no promised order. */
  inFlight(): Promise<Message[]>;
  /** Deliver one message in transit, by its id. */
  deliver(id: string): Promise<void>;
  /** Deliver every message in transit, and every message those deliveries send, until none is left. */
  deliverAll(): Promise<void>;
}

/** The outcome of a command: it took effect, or it was refused and changed nothing. */
export type Outcome = { ok: true } | { ok: false; reason: string };

export interface OrderView {
  status: 'pending' | 'confirmed' | 'rejected' | 'cancelling' | 'cancelled' | 'expired';
  qty: number;
}

export interface Host extends Network {
  place(order: string, qty: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  cancel(order: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  expire(order: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  restock(): Promise<Outcome>;
  /** The order, or null when no order has that id. */
  order(order: string): Promise<OrderView | null>;
  stock(): Promise<{ available: number; reserved: number }>;
}

/** The module's default export: a factory of a fresh system, with the inventory and no orders. */
export type CreateHost = () => Promise<Host>;
```

Update your delivery to satisfy the brief as changed, keeping everything the change does not touch. Test your work as you go. When you are done, say so in one line.

